segregation in reactors', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Chemical Reaction Engineering', 'Technical Concept', 'Separation or non-uniform distribution of phases or species in a reactor, including its effects on transport, reaction rates, residence-time behaviour, and reactor performance.', 'Curricular scope: Chemical Reaction Engineering. The concept is represented at the level of the stated mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria.', 'Key elements: Phase segregation in reactors; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria.', 'Canonical knowledge concept for Phase segregation in reactors; primary curricular occurrence: Chemical Reaction Engineering.', 'Phase segregation in reactors; Key elements: Phase segregation in reactors; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria; Chemical Reaction Engineering', 'Active'), ('KCR_001256', 'Soil permeability', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Foundation Engineering', 'Technical Concept', 'Property describing the ability of soil to transmit fluid through its interconnected pore space under a hydraulic gradient; commonly represented by hydraulic conductivity in saturated flow analysis.', 'Curricular scope: Foundation Engineering. The concept is represented at the level of the stated mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria.', 'Key elements: Soil permeability; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria.', 'Canonical knowledge concept for Soil permeability; primary curricular occurrence: Foundation Engineering.', 'Soil permeability; Key elements: Soil permeability; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria; Foundation Engineering', 'Active'), ('KCR_001257', 'Membrane permeability', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Mass Transfer Operations', 'Technical Concept', 'Permeability of a membrane to a specified component or species, governing the rate at which that component passes through the membrane under a specified driving force.', 'Curricular scope: Mass Transfer Operations. The concept is represented at the level of the stated mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria.', 'Key elements: Membrane permeability; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria.', 'Canonical knowledge concept for Membrane permeability; primary curricular occurrence: Mass Transfer Operations.', 'Membrane permeability; Key elements: Membrane permeability; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria; Mass Transfer Operations', 'Active'), ('KCR_001258', 'Reactor mixing', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Chemical Reaction Engineering', 'Technical Concept', 'Mixing of reactants and fluid phases within a chemical reactor to reduce concentration and temperature gradients and influence transport, reaction rate, selectivity, and residence-time behaviour.', 'Curricular scope: Chemical Reaction Engineering. The concept is represented at the level of the stated mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria.', 'Key elements: Reactor mixing; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria.', 'Canonical knowledge concept for Reactor mixing; primary curricular occurrence: Chemical Reaction Engineering.', 'Reactor mixing; Key elements: Reactor mixing; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria; Chemical Reaction Engineering', 'Active'), ('KCR_001259', 'Geotechnical sampling', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Foundation Engineering', 'Technical Concept', 'Collection of representative soil, rock, groundwater, or other subsurface samples for laboratory characterization and design decisions, with attention to sample disturbance and representativeness.', 'Curricular scope: Foundation Engineering. The concept is represented at the level of the stated mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria.', 'Key elements: Geotechnical sampling; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria.', 'Canonical knowledge concept for Geotechnical sampling; primary curricular occurrence: Foundation Engineering.', 'Geotechnical sampling; Key elements: Geotechnical sampling; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria; Foundation Engineering', 'Active'), ('KCR_001260', 'Signal sampling', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Mechatronics; Electrical Measurements and Instrumentation', 'Technical Concept', 'Conversion of a continuous-time signal into discrete samples at specified sampling instants; sampling rate and reconstruction requirements determine aliasing and information loss.', 'Curricular scope: Mechatronics; Electrical Measurements and Instrumentation. The concept is represented at the level of the stated mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria.', 'Key elements: Signal sampling; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria.', 'Canonical knowledge concept for Signal sampling; primary curricular occurrence: Mechatronics; Electrical Measurements and Instrumentation.', 'Signal sampling; Key elements: Signal sampling; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria; Mechatronics; Electrical Measurements and Instrumentation', 'Active'), ('KCR_001261', 'Air infiltration', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Refrigeration and Air Conditioning', 'Technical Concept', 'Uncontrolled or unintended entry of outdoor air into a conditioned space through leakage paths driven by pressure differences, wind, stack effect, or mechanical-system operation.', 'Curricular scope: Refrigeration and Air Conditioning. The concept is represented at the level of the stated mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria.', 'Key elements: Air infiltration; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria.', 'Canonical knowledge concept for Air infiltration; primary curricular occurrence: Refrigeration and Air Conditioning.', 'Air infiltration; Key elements: Air infiltration; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria; Refrigeration and Air Conditioning', 'Active'), ('KCR_001262', 'Reactor ignition', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Chemical Reaction Engineering', 'Technical Concept', 'Onset of self-sustained combustion or rapid exothermic reaction in a reactive mixture when thermal and kinetic conditions permit ignition or autoignition.', 'Curricular scope: Chemical Reaction Engineering. The concept is represented at the level of the stated mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria.', 'Key elements: Reactor ignition; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria.', 'Canonical knowledge concept for Reactor ignition; primary curricular occurrence: Chemical Reaction Engineering.', 'Reactor ignition; Key elements: Reactor ignition; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria; Chemical Reaction Engineering', 'Active'), ('KCR_001263', 'Membrane selectivity', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Mass Transfer Operations', 'Technical Concept', 'Degree to which a membrane preferentially permeates one component relative to another, determined by differences in sorption and transport properties and expressed through appropriate selectivity metrics.', 'Curricular scope: Mass Transfer Operations. The concept is represented at the level of the stated mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria.', 'Key elements: Membrane selectivity; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria.', 'Canonical knowledge concept for Membrane selectivity; primary curricular occurrence: Mass Transfer Operations.', 'Membrane selectivity; Key elements: Membrane selectivity; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria; Mass Transfer Operations', 'Active'), ('KCR_001264', 'Measurement sensitivity', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Electrical Measurements and Instrumentation', 'Technical Concept', 'Change in measurement-system output per unit change in the measurand or input quantity, considered together with resolution, noise, range, and uncertainty when evaluating an instrument.', 'Curricular scope: Electrical Measurements and Instrumentation. The concept is represented at the level of the stated mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria.', 'Key elements: Measurement sensitivity; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria.', 'Canonical knowledge concept for Measurement sensitivity; primary curricular occurrence: Electrical Measurements and Instrumentation.', 'Measurement sensitivity; Key elements: Measurement sensitivity; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria; Electrical Measurements and Instrumentation', 'Active'), ('KCR_001265', 'Policy coordination', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Public Policy and Governance', 'Technical Concept', 'Alignment of actions, responsibilities, instruments, and decisions among public institutions or policy actors to reduce conflict, duplication, and implementation gaps.', 'Curricular scope: Public Policy and Governance. The concept is represented at the level of the stated mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria.', 'Key elements: Policy coordination; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria.', 'Canonical knowledge concept for Policy coordination; primary curricular occurrence: Public Policy and Governance.', 'Policy coordination; Key elements: Policy coordination; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria; Public Policy and Governance', 'Active'), ('KCR_001266', 'Research confidentiality', 'Law', 'Research Methods in Social Sciences', 'Legal Concept', 'Protection of identifiable or sensitive research information from unauthorized access or disclosure, consistent with informed consent, ethics requirements, data-management plans, and applicable law.', 'Curricular scope: Research Methods in Social Sciences. The concept is represented at the level of the stated mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria.', 'Key elements: Research confidentiality; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria.', 'Canonical knowledge concept for Research confidentiality; primary curricular occurrence: Research Methods in Social Sciences.', 'Research confidentiality; Key elements: Research confidentiality; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria; Research Methods in Social Sciences', 'Active'), ('KCR_001267', 'Engine calibration', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Internal Combustion Engines', 'Technical Concept', 'Adjustment and validation of engine control parameters and maps so that the engine meets specified performance, emissions, drivability, and operating constraints across its intended operating range.', 'Internal Combustion Engines → Engine Control and Diagnostics: calibration of control parameters and maps, validation against performance and emissions constraints, and operating-range considerations.', 'Calibration targets; parameter/map adjustment; operating-point coverage; performance and emissions constraints; validation and trade-offs.', 'Canonical engine-control calibration concept; distinct from metrological calibration of measurement instruments.', 'engine calibration; engine control calibration; Calibration targets; parameter/map adjustment; operating-point coverage; performance and emissions constraints', 'Active') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;